======================================================================
(A) The upper-bound 7 = the Eisenstein prime above 7
======================================================================
  N(3 + w) = 3^2 - 3*1 + 1^2 = 7   (the prime above 7)
  7 splits in Z[w] iff 7 = 1 mod 3:  7 mod 3 = 1  -> splits
  smallest Eisenstein norms (Loeschian numbers) up to 13:
    [1, 3, 4, 7, 9, 12, 13]
    -> 3 (ramified, triangular-lattice 3-coloring), then 4, then 7.
    7 is the first SPLIT prime; its quotient Z[w]/(3+w) = F_7.

  w == -3 == 4 (mod 7);  check w^2+w+1 = 0 (mod 7)
  6 Eisenstein units mod 7 = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]  == F_7* = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
  closed hexagon nbhd (center 0 + 6 units) = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] == all of F_7
  evaluation point 2: 2^2+2+1 = 0 (mod 7) -> 2 is ALSO a cube root
  the two primitive cube roots of unity mod 7 are 2 and 4 = 2^2; 2*4=1

======================================================================
(B) Robustness of ONE hexagonal 7-coloring (forbidden-distance interval)
======================================================================
  hexagon circumradius R = 1.0
  forbidden monochromatic-distance interval: ( 2.0000 , 2.5826 )
  robustness ratio (hi/lo) = (sqrt(21)-2)/2 = 1.29129
  -> setting unit distance =1 works for R in (1/2.5826, 1/2.0000)
     = ( 0.3872 , 0.5000 )   (diameter 2R in (0.7744, 1.0000))
  So a single 7-coloring kills a whole BAND of distances, ratio ~1.29:
  this slack is exactly why 7 is not known to be tight (room to merge colors).

======================================================================
(C) The density barrier: why 1/m1 caps at 5, never 6
======================================================================
  known: 0.2293 <= m1 <= 0.2598  (classical) / <= 0.247 (recent LP)
  density bound chi >= ceil(1/m1):
    1/m1 ranges in [1/0.2598, 1/0.2293] = [3.849, 4.361]
    reaching 5 is THRESHOLD-DEPENDENT: 1/0.2598=3.85<4 (only >=4);
                                       1/0.247=4.05>4 (gives >=5).
    (the PROVEN chi_m>=5 is Falconer 1981, a refined, not single-class, argument)
  THE ROBUST BARRIER (m1-bound-INDEPENDENT): chi >= 6 is IMPOSSIBLE here.
    need m1 < 1/6 = 0.1667, but the Croft set has density 0.2293 > 0.1667.
    so 1/m1 <= 4.361 < 6 ALWAYS, regardless of the m1 upper bound.
  => the single-class density (= LRC lonely-density) bound is PROVABLY capped
     below 6; the {5,6,7} distinction is irreducibly combinatorial (de Grey
     graphs / multi-class LP), not single-class density. = the LRC Vitali wall.

  This is the plane mirror of LRC(14): the first-moment/density bound is
  vacuous past a point; the content lives in arc CORRELATIONS (HYP-2195).
